==Tok Pisin==

===Etymology===
Cognate to {{etyl|bi|-}} {{term|bensin||petrol|lang=bi}} (a term which entered {{etyl|bi|-}} pre-1885). According to Terry Crowley, the term derives either from {{etyl|de|tpi}} {{term|Benzin|lang=de}}, or from {{etyl|en|tpi}} {{term|benzene|lang=en}}, as the meaning of that term was not as narrow or technical in the nineteenth century as it is today.<ref>Terry Crowley, ''Beach-la-Mar to Bislama: the emergence of a national language in Vanuatu'' (1990), page 137.</ref>

